[2026-08-08 18:10:26] ARCHITECT: MECH C = frontier_memory_v2 (H1 NOISE test). Calibrated the parked frontier_memory per CHAINING_REPORT prescriptions: (1) success-gated credit - penalize a cell ONLY when its episode failed AND never approached the goal (best_dist > APPROACH=4; success is proxied by approach because env_maze never exposes the episode outcome to the choose_action hook, and any episode that gets within APPROACH cells must have had the goal in view and auto-stepped to it, so never-approach is a conservative failure proxy that under-penalizes); (2) MIN_CONF=2 independent never-approach episodes before any penalty weight is applied, killing the single-unlucky-episode damage (v1 min -0.53 per-seed maze delta); (3) BETA 0.10 -> 0.03. Prediction: maze primary +0.02..+0.08 (aggregate +0.8%..+3.2%), sd still > mean but far tighter than v1; clears +5% ONLY if the maze headroom (+8% max) is largely real and capturable.
[2026-08-08 18:10:26] ARCHITECT: MECH D = evidence_substrate (H2 CEILING test). REACHABILITY AUDIT (honest): the runner fires before_eval/choose_action/after_write today; retrieve fires ONLY for SelfLab AND ONLY with attention_budget active - it is PARKED, so SelfLab is genuinely UNREACHABLE by any new mechanism (a retrieve hook would be dead code). Second contract fact: env_maze calls choose_action WITHOUT the atomspace, so a mechanism's maze state is ctx-local per seed; env_repoops DOES hand after_write the atomspace. Multi-domain design therefore = one module, two hooks, one shared reliability primitive (per-identity empirical residuals) stored ctx-local for maze and in atomspace for repoops: after_write re-applies the per-feature EMA residual (the residual_bias recipe that reached +2.8% agg) and choose_action applies the calibrated confirmation-gated maze re-ranking (the H1 recipe). Prediction: repoops +0.03..+0.07 and maze +0.02..+0.05 combine to +2%..+5.5% - the only class that straddles the +5% gate.
[2026-08-08 18:10:26] GOVERNOR: phase3-cycle-3 frontier_memory_v2 = PARK (21-seed binding). before=0.8847 after=0.8970 rel=+1.4% rob=+0.0000; 7-seed +0.6% PARK. Maze primary 0.8229 -> 0.8538 (+0.0309), per-seed mean=+0.0308 sd=0.1146 min=-0.1187 max=+0.5101, positive 11/21 negative 5/21. vs v1: maze delta doubled (+0.0141 -> +0.0309), downside contained (-0.526 -> -0.119), but sd 0.115 still > mean 0.031 and aggregate +1.4% is nowhere near +5%. H1 STRONG FORM REFUTED: the calibration recovered ~2.2x the maze gain and removed the catastrophic-seed damage, but the park was NOT purely a calibration artifact - even calibrated, the effect is sub-threshold and variance-dominated. The +8% maze headroom is mathematically real but only ~17% of it is practically capturable by this mechanism class.
[2026-08-08 18:10:26] GOVERNOR: phase3-cycle-4 evidence_substrate = PARK (21-seed binding). before=0.8847 after=0.9220 rel=+4.2% rob=+0.0952 (robustness IMPROVED); 7-seed +4.9% PARK. Per-domain: maze +0.0309, repoops +0.0714 (0.9167 -> 0.9881, 95% of the hard repoops ceiling), selflab 0.0000. This is the LARGEST honest aggregate gain measured in ANY phase (phase-1 +12.1% was from the empty baseline, a different test) and it still does NOT clear +5%. A well-designed two-hook multi-domain mechanism captured the entire repoops ceiling AND a real maze gain and landed at +4.2% - within 0.8 points of the gate. Per the H2 decision rule, H2's strong form (multi-domain promotes) FAILS; the gate/weighting design is therefore the BINDING CONSTRAINT (design-level finding).
[2026-08-08 18:10:26] GOVERNOR: SYNTHESIS (phase 3). No second-order promotion for the third phase in a row. Actual verdicts: residual_bias +2.8%, frontier_memory +0.6%, frontier_memory_v2 +1.4%, evidence_substrate +4.2% - ALL PARK. COUNTERFACTUAL (offline, measured numbers only): under a per-domain gate (ANY domain >= +5% rel AND no domain > -3% drop), residual_bias AND evidence_substrate would PROMOTE (both carried repoops +7.8% relative within-domain); equal-1/3 weights promote 0/4; headroom-proportional weights promote 0/4; only the two repoops-capable candidates could clear +5% under ANY weight config, and only at repoops weight >= 0.62. => The 3-phase stall is a RULE-DESIGN problem (the single aggregate gate hides large within-domain gains), not a mechanism problem.
