[2026-08-08 18:40:00] ARCHITECT: phase5 mech=progress_thermostat (maze-only within-episode explore/exploit thermostat). DESIGN RATIONALE: incumbent [uncertainty_planning, residual_bias] has RepoOps saturated (0.9881) and SelfLab unreachable (retrieve hook only fires with parked attention_budget). UNCLAIMED headroom = Maze (0.8229, weight 0.40). Trace-verified failure mode: on hard mazes (seed 101 maze 1) the agent reaches within 3 cells of the goal (step 29, best_dist=3), then uncertainty_planning keeps committing to far info-gain cells, drifts to dist 7+, and burns the 95-step budget on all 5 episodes. ORTHOGONALITY ARGUMENT: uncertainty_planning is a STATELESS scorer (same ranking for same map, no memory of the episode, constant 0.7/goal_dist term). progress_thermostat is a STATEFUL within-episode control layer that switches the OBJECTIVE (explore->exploit) based on goal-proximity trajectory - a quantity the stateless scorer cannot see. It defers 100% to uncertainty_planning when far from goal; near-goal (<=5) it re-orders the SAME candidate cells by goal proximity, and a drift safety valve pulls back if the agent wanders >3 beyond its best approach. NOT a re-tune of frontier_memory (no cross-episode credit, no learned weights, no episode-boundary processing). NOT residual_bias territory (no after_write hook, zero repoops effect). SelfLab honest note: only reachable hooks are before_eval/choose_action/after_write; a selflab effect is not honestly reachable without attention_budget, so target is maze-only.
